/* W06.A.2 — minimal version definition for the LD_PRELOAD shim.
 *
 * The `.symver` inline-assembly directives in src/lib.rs tag each
 * libc interposer with `@FBSD_1.0` so FreeBSD base utilities
 * (install, mv, cp, etc.) — which import libc symbols as
 * versioned `open@FBSD_1.0`, `unlink@FBSD_1.0`, etc. — bind their
 * PLT slots to our shim.
 *
 * lld refuses to emit a symbol tagged `@FBSD_1.0` unless a
 * version *definition* by that name exists in `.gnu.version_d`.
 * This script provides that definition. It deliberately lists NO
 * symbols — rustc auto-generates its own version script
 * (anonymous, with `local: *;`) listing every `#[no_mangle] pub`
 * symbol as global. Lld merges this script with rustc's. If we
 * listed symbols here, lld would error with "anonymous +
 * named version combination" because two version scripts can't
 * have differently-named blocks.
 *
 * The empty body `{ };` just declares the version name. lld then
 * matches the `.symver`-emitted versioned symbols against it.
 */
FBSD_1.0 { };
